HelixAngleCalc[eigenvectors, mask, maskp, vox] calculates the helix angle \
matrix of cardiac data using only a left ventricle mask, and a maskp for \
visualization.\nHelixAngleCalc[eigenvectors, mask, centerpoint, vec, inout, \
vox]  calculates the helix angle matrix of cardiac data using only a left \
ventricle mask.\nHelixAngleCalc[eigenvectors, mask, maskp, centerpoint, vec, \
inout, vox] calculates the helix angle matrix of cardiac data using a left \
vantricle mask and a maskp for visualization.\n\neigenvectors are the tensor \
eigenvectors calculated with EigenvecCalc.\nmask is a mask of the left \
ventricle.\nmaskp is a mask used for visualization.\nvox is the voxels size, \
{slice, x, y}.\n\nThe folowing values are calculated automaticlay Using \
CentralAxes but can also be provided as an input.\ncenterpoint is the center \
of each slice calculated with CentralAxes.\ninout is the inner and outer \
